@@ -0,0 +1,11 @@
+# Plan
+
+## 1. Tests
+
+- [ ] 1.1 A build whose entry imports the same asset as `?url&marker=value` and `?url&marker=other` passes each query to renderBuiltUrl, so the entry chunk holds both rendered URLs (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/build.spec.ts) [AC-1]
+- [ ] 1.2 The same build with a stylesheet whose url() references carry the two queries passes each query to renderBuiltUrl, so the CSS asset holds both rendered URLs (packages/vite/src/node/__tests__/build.spec.ts) [AC-2]
+
+## 2. Fix
+
+- [ ] 2.1 Store an asset reference's query and hash in its URL metadata under a urlId, and carry the urlId in the `import.meta.ROLLDOWN_FILE_URL_*` expression and the `__VITE_ASSET__` token (packages/vite/src/node/plugins/asset.ts)
+- [ ] 2.2 Append the stored postfix to the filename passed to renderBuiltUrl when a file URL or a token is resolved (packages/vite/src/node/plugins/asset.ts, packages/vite/src/node/plugins/css.ts)
